00:05:33.932 --> 00:05:35.790
(bright, quaint piano music)

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:38.010
There's a bunch of powerful
American companies here,

00:05:38.010 --> 00:05:41.070
but a new president comes to
power, vowing to regulate them.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:42.810
The US is not gonna let this happen.

00:05:42.810 --> 00:05:45.090
So the Secretary of State
starts spreading rumors

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:46.890
to smear this guy, this president,

00:05:46.890 --> 00:05:48.240
saying that he's building a canal

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:50.280
that would compete with the Panama Canal.

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:51.780
But really they're just upset because

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:54.150
Nicaragua was taking loans from Europe.

00:05:54.150 --> 00:05:56.550
The US keeps painting
this guy as a war criminal

00:05:56.550 --> 00:05:58.500
and someone worthy of being thrown out.

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:02.640
So, push comes to shove

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:05.670
and the US sends ships to
both of Nicaragua's coasts.

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:08.040
They assemble a bunch
of Marines in Panama,

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:10.560
basically just flexing on Nicaragua

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:12.750
and telling the president to step down.

00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:15.057
And the benefit of being a
rising superpower is that

00:06:15.057 --> 00:06:18.120
it worked, he has no
choice but to step down.

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:21.180
And soon a leader that the
US likes comes to power.

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:22.350
The coup is complete.

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:24.780
And really, this is the
first of many instances of

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:26.730
the US meddling in Nicaragua.

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:28.890
A few years later, the
US is back in the region

00:06:28.890 --> 00:06:31.560
for another coup in next door Honduras.

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:34.530
This one was plotted by a band
of private American citizens

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:35.970
and it follows a similar pattern.

00:06:35.970 --> 00:06:37.320
A new president comes to town,

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:39.750
in this case directly inspired
by Nicaragua's president,

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:41.850
and he wants to take back
control of the country

00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:43.290
from American businesses.

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:45.150
In this case we're talking about bananas.

00:06:45.150 --> 00:06:47.280
The banana companies were
not gonna let this happen.

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:48.840
And it was mostly this guy,

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:51.660
a banana businessman
named Sam the Banana Man.

00:06:51.660 --> 00:06:54.960
He's not gonna let this pesky
president run his country, no.

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:56.473
So he assembles his own militia,

00:06:56.473 --> 00:06:59.730
he literally buys a surplus Navy ship,

00:06:59.730 --> 00:07:00.816
loads it up with weapons,

00:07:00.816 --> 00:07:03.840
and starts his campaign
to get this president out.

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:06.150
He sails from New Orleans
to the coast of Honduras

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:07.800
and he literally invades the country

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:09.720
with, like, a private army.

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:12.000
Wait, what? Where's the
US government in all this?

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:12.930
They also didn't like

00:07:12.930 --> 00:07:14.760
the political direction
of Honduras either.

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:16.590
So they just sort of stood back,

00:07:16.590 --> 00:07:18.600
let this private invasion happen.

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:20.190
And then at the critical moment,

00:07:20.190 --> 00:07:22.560
the US steps in to order a ceasefire,

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:25.110
basically bullying the
president to step down.

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:29.170
He had no way forward, no
defense, so he resigns.

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:30.990
(urgent synth music)

00:07:30.990 --> 00:07:34.230
And the Banana Man's leader of
choice takes the presidency,

00:07:34.230 --> 00:07:37.200
giving the banana businessman
land and a unique status

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:39.614
to import anything he needs tax free

00:07:39.614 --> 00:07:42.660
and, wait for it, he refunds him

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:47.550
for all of the coup expenses
using public Honduran money.

00:07:47.550 --> 00:07:49.830
This Banana Man literally
overthrew the government

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:53.043
and made Honduras pay for it. Wow.

00:07:54.034 --> 00:07:56.340
Okay, so let's move
forward to the '50s where

00:07:56.340 --> 00:08:00.390
the coup becomes a more useful
tool in the American toolkit.

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:01.800
There's this new US agency

00:08:01.800 --> 00:08:04.290
dedicated to collecting
and analyzing information

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:07.110
from all over the world,
meaning for spying.

00:08:07.110 --> 00:08:10.410
They call it the Central
Intelligence Agency, the CIA.

00:08:10.410 --> 00:08:12.990
And it completely revolutionizes
the art of the coup.

00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:13.830
Oh, and at this point,

00:08:13.830 --> 00:08:16.380
the US is now a full-blown
global superpower.

00:08:16.380 --> 00:08:18.750
No longer just looking in
their own neighborhood,

00:08:18.750 --> 00:08:20.670
but rather at the whole world map,

00:08:20.670 --> 00:08:22.500
investing huge resources into

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:25.593
fighting their global rival
and its communist ideology.

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:32.660
So this gets us to Iran 1953,
where Iran had just elected

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:35.910
a new star politician, Mohammed Mosaddegh.

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:37.290
He rises the power believing that

00:08:37.290 --> 00:08:39.150
Iran must take back control of

00:08:39.150 --> 00:08:41.730
its most valuable natural resource, oil,

00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:43.740
which at the time was
completely controlled by

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:46.590
a British company called the
Anglo-Iranian Oil Company.

00:08:46.590 --> 00:08:48.540
We know it today as BP.

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:49.567
Mosaddegh is done with this.

00:08:49.567 --> 00:08:51.780
"Let's kick the British
out and take back our oil."

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:53.886
But like the US, Britain is not happy with

00:08:53.886 --> 00:08:56.190
Iranians trying to take
back their resources.

00:08:56.190 --> 00:08:57.780
So they warn that if they do this,

00:08:57.780 --> 00:08:59.403
there will be consequences.

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:02.610
So the British catch a quick meeting

00:09:02.610 --> 00:09:04.170
with the CIA's Middle East guy,

00:09:04.170 --> 00:09:05.910
who was passing through London,

00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:07.687
and they pitch him on this idea.

00:09:07.687 --> 00:09:09.780
"Let's throw out Mosaddegh."

00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:11.550
The CIA's like, "Okay."

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:14.220
And they kind of sniff
communist vibes on Mosaddegh

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:17.130
with this big desire to
nationalize Iran's oil.

00:09:17.130 --> 00:09:18.870
Or at least they tell themselves they do.

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:22.410
So the CIA agrees, and they
secretly send this guy to Iran.

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:24.870
He's the Middle East Bureau
chief, Kermit Roosevelt,

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:26.130
he's like in his thirties.

00:09:26.130 --> 00:09:28.380
Oh, and yes, he is the grandson of

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:30.300
another big coup guy, Teddy Roosevelt,

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:32.700
who I have gone into in other videos.

00:09:32.700 --> 00:09:34.410
Roosevelt sneaks into Iran

00:09:34.410 --> 00:09:37.747
and is given a million
taxpayer dollars to use, quote,

00:09:37.747 --> 00:09:41.100
"in any way that would bring
about the fall of Mosaddegh."

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:43.235
So now there's American CIA agents in Iran

00:09:43.235 --> 00:09:45.570
secretly trying to
overthrow the government.

00:09:45.570 --> 00:09:48.192
And it's a rocky start at
first, with a bunch of failures.

00:09:48.192 --> 00:09:50.730
But they start using their
money to get traction,

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:53.460
bribing politicians, religious
clerics, and other leaders

00:09:53.460 --> 00:09:56.220
to say divisive and controversial
things about Mosaddegh.

00:09:56.220 --> 00:10:00.000
They hire locals to stage attacks
against religious leaders,

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:00.960
making it look like

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:03.000
they had been ordered
to do so by Mosaddegh,

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:05.430
but really, they were getting
paid by the CIA to do this.

00:10:05.430 --> 00:10:06.600
And with enough time and money,

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:09.540
they create an atmosphere
of chaos and hostility

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:11.580
and distrust among the public.

00:10:11.580 --> 00:10:12.750
Oh, and there's weapons.

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:16.230
The CIA stashes enough weapons
and explosives to support

00:10:16.230 --> 00:10:20.190
a, quote, "10,000 man guerilla
organization for six months."

00:10:20.190 --> 00:10:23.430
Like, just in case they need
to start a full-on conflict.

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:24.677
The result of all of this is

00:10:24.677 --> 00:10:27.900
more violence and chaos
that engulfs the capitol.

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:30.491
Shops are being destroyed,
bullets are flying into mosques,

00:10:30.491 --> 00:10:32.250
people are beaten,

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:35.017
and thousands of paid
demonstrators flood the street.

00:10:35.017 --> 00:10:37.170
The city falls into anarchy,

00:10:37.170 --> 00:10:39.510
all of it orchestrated by CIA money.

00:10:39.510 --> 00:10:41.460
And in the end, this all results in

00:10:41.460 --> 00:10:43.740
a bloody shootout at Mosaddegh's house.

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:45.990
He eventually gives up
and turns himself in.

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:49.530
He's put through a sham trial
and found guilty of treason

00:10:49.530 --> 00:10:52.206
and sentenced to three years
in solitary confinement

00:10:52.206 --> 00:10:55.290
and then house arrest, where
he stayed until his death.

00:10:55.290 --> 00:10:56.880
The previous ruler of Iran,

00:10:56.880 --> 00:10:59.070
Mohammed Reza Shah,
which just means "King,"

00:10:59.070 --> 00:11:00.600
had fled the country.

00:11:00.600 --> 00:11:03.052
But now, with the democratically
elected Mosaddegh gone

00:11:03.052 --> 00:11:05.580
and with the backing of the US and UK,

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:09.270
he could charter a flight back
into Iran and take control.

00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:11.010
- [TV Reporter] The Shah crowns himself

00:11:11.010 --> 00:11:14.100
in a tradition which
goes back 25 centuries.

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:15.732
His title is King of Kings,

00:11:15.732 --> 00:11:17.839
and he becomes emperor of his nation.

00:11:17.839 --> 00:11:18.672
(suspenseful string music)

00:11:18.672 --> 00:11:20.310
- [Narrator] The US really
came out on top here.

00:11:20.310 --> 00:11:21.390
They got what they wanted.

00:11:21.390 --> 00:11:23.310
They now have an
American-friendly dictator

00:11:23.310 --> 00:11:25.170
in a powerful country in the Middle East

00:11:25.170 --> 00:11:27.162
who is now welcoming
American oil companies

00:11:27.162 --> 00:11:30.561
to get in on one of the
largest oil reserves on Earth.

00:11:30.561 --> 00:11:33.780
Under the Shaw, Iran becomes
a brutal police state.

00:11:33.780 --> 00:11:36.450
He executed military
officers, student leaders,

00:11:36.450 --> 00:11:38.250
anyone associated with Mosaddegh.

00:11:38.250 --> 00:11:41.070
He set up a secret police
force, and life was brutal.

00:11:41.070 --> 00:11:45.000
So brutal that in 1979,
the frustration of Iranians

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:46.830
burst forth in mass protests

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:48.270
that ran the Shaw out of office

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:50.760
and replaced him with
an inspiring new leader

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:53.122
who would turn Iran
into an Islamic Republic

00:11:53.122 --> 00:11:55.920
built in part off a
foundation of resentment

00:11:55.920 --> 00:11:58.590
for the US having
meddled in their country.

00:11:58.590 --> 00:12:01.230
The Islamic Republic has
held power ever since,

00:12:01.230 --> 00:12:04.317
and has morphed into the
oppressive theocracy we know today,

00:12:04.317 --> 00:12:06.303
though maybe not for long.

00:12:08.970 --> 00:12:11.940
Before we go on, a quick
reminder that all of these coups,

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:15.300
these plans to overthrow
leaders in other countries,

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:18.150
did not require American
votes or consensus

00:12:18.150 --> 00:12:19.650
or approval of Congress.

00:12:19.650 --> 00:12:21.241
It was usually just a few key men

00:12:21.241 --> 00:12:23.640
in government buildings in Washington DC

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:24.810
making this happen.

00:12:24.810 --> 00:12:27.090
These people would go on
to define the Cold War

00:12:27.090 --> 00:12:30.270
and shape so many covert
operations around the world,

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:32.593
many of which we'll never know about.

00:12:32.593 --> 00:12:34.320
Okay, let's keep going.
(urgent drum music)

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:35.910
The next year in Guatemala,

00:12:35.910 --> 00:12:38.100
the CIA tried to pull the same playbook

00:12:38.100 --> 00:12:39.390
that they used in Iran,

00:12:39.390 --> 00:12:42.240
once again targeting a leader
that the people had elected,

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:44.640
but who wanted to take back
the country's resources

00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:45.570
for the people,

00:12:45.570 --> 00:12:47.310
to break up these American monopolies

00:12:47.310 --> 00:12:50.130
that controlled the country's
electricity and railroad.

00:12:50.130 --> 00:12:52.170
The president even starts to seize land

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:54.210
from one massive banana company.

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:56.280
It was often unused land that
he wanted to redistribute

00:12:56.280 --> 00:12:59.258
to the locals who could farm
it and feed their families

00:12:59.258 --> 00:13:00.630
and hopefully climb out of

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:03.180
the system of endemic
poverty in the country.

00:13:03.180 --> 00:13:04.620
Once again, I made a whole video on this,

00:13:04.620 --> 00:13:07.590
the geopolitics of bananas
in Central America.

00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:09.660
But the fact is that the US decided that

00:13:09.660 --> 00:13:11.850
they had to defend the banana companies

00:13:11.850 --> 00:13:15.180
or else more communist
reforms would spread.

00:13:15.180 --> 00:13:17.310
So the US president and secretary of state

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:18.840
ordered an overthrow,

00:13:18.840 --> 00:13:20.640
and the CIA got right to work.

00:13:20.640 --> 00:13:23.454
The CIA hand selects a leader
that they want to be in power

00:13:23.454 --> 00:13:26.400
and then they start giving
equipment and training to

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:29.610
a bunch of Guatemalan
exiles and private soldiers.

00:13:29.610 --> 00:13:31.470
They set up a secret operation base

00:13:31.470 --> 00:13:33.120
on the outskirts of Miami.

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:35.358
They start delivering
weapons to the Panama Canal.

00:13:35.358 --> 00:13:36.600
But like the other coups,

00:13:36.600 --> 00:13:38.730
it can't just all be about weapons.

00:13:38.730 --> 00:13:40.740
They gotta own the information space.

00:13:40.740 --> 00:13:42.363
So they create a radio station

00:13:42.363 --> 00:13:45.690
that sounds like it's a local
Guatemala radio station,

00:13:45.690 --> 00:13:47.100
but really it's being operated

00:13:47.100 --> 00:13:48.720
out of a small town in Florida.

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:50.280
And they start publishing fake news

00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:53.130
about an uprising, unrest, a rebellion.

00:13:53.130 --> 00:13:54.390
And then at the same time,

00:13:54.390 --> 00:13:57.060
the fighters that the
CIA had trained and armed

00:13:57.060 --> 00:13:58.590
invades Guatemala.

00:13:58.590 --> 00:14:00.300
Pilots start dropping bombs

00:14:00.300 --> 00:14:03.090
on fuel tanks and military
posts and airports.

00:14:03.090 --> 00:14:05.250
But they weren't starting a full-on war.

00:14:05.250 --> 00:14:06.900
They weren't trying to cause real damage.

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:09.810
They wanted it to feel
like a domestic uprising,

00:14:09.810 --> 00:14:11.640
like a war was on the horizon,

00:14:11.640 --> 00:14:14.640
to freak people out, and
for many it totally worked.

00:14:14.640 --> 00:14:16.770
They thought that this was a real uprising

00:14:16.770 --> 00:14:19.800
and had no idea that the
CIA was behind it all.

00:14:19.800 --> 00:14:21.600
But the president knew what was up.

00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:24.750
He had messed with the USA
and now he's hearing about it.

00:14:24.750 --> 00:14:27.330
Military leaders in his circle
are feeling the pressure

00:14:27.330 --> 00:14:28.830
from the big bully from the north

00:14:28.830 --> 00:14:31.800
and they turn on him and
he eventually surrenders.

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:34.410
On his way out, the president
addresses his people,

00:14:34.410 --> 00:14:35.887
makes it very clear that, quote,

00:14:35.887 --> 00:14:37.530
"The United Fruit Company,

00:14:37.530 --> 00:14:39.660
in collaboration with the United States,

00:14:39.660 --> 00:14:42.120
is responsible for what
is happening to us."

00:14:42.120 --> 00:14:44.310
And just like that, one president is out

00:14:44.310 --> 00:14:47.010
and the handpicked CIA option is in.

00:14:47.010 --> 00:14:50.022
This new regime is brutal and
goes on to do horrible things,

00:14:50.022 --> 00:14:52.380
detaining people they
thought were communists,

00:14:52.380 --> 00:14:55.110
killing prisoners,
breaking up labor unions,

00:14:55.110 --> 00:14:58.170
and in the process restoring
the banana company's land

00:14:58.170 --> 00:14:59.670
and ensuring that they maintained

00:14:59.670 --> 00:15:01.140
their hold on this economy.

00:15:01.140 --> 00:15:03.030
This kicks off an era in Guatemala

00:15:03.030 --> 00:15:05.850
of more political
assassinations and instability,

00:15:05.850 --> 00:15:07.860
something that still
plagues the country today.

00:15:07.860 --> 00:15:10.080
And yet to this day,
there is no evidence that

00:15:10.080 --> 00:15:13.140
the Soviets were ever slightly
interested in Guatemala.

00:15:13.140 --> 00:15:15.150
Communism was once again the excuse,

00:15:15.150 --> 00:15:16.290
but really this was about

00:15:16.290 --> 00:15:18.360
securing American business interests,

00:15:18.360 --> 00:15:21.050
tearing a country apart for bananas.

00:15:21.050 --> 00:15:26.050
♪ Bananas taste the best
and are the best for you ♪

00:15:26.760 --> 00:15:28.230
All right, let's go to Africa.

00:15:28.230 --> 00:15:30.120
So, it's 1960 here in
the center of Africa,

00:15:30.120 --> 00:15:31.982
a country called Congo.

00:15:31.982 --> 00:15:34.260
They just gained
independence from Belgium,

00:15:34.260 --> 00:15:35.220
and they have an election,

00:15:35.220 --> 00:15:37.380
and this guy Patrice Lumumbau wins,

00:15:37.380 --> 00:15:38.490
becomes the prime minister.

00:15:38.490 --> 00:15:40.410
But immediately, over in Washington,

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:43.165
the communist alarm bells
instantly start sounding off,

00:15:43.165 --> 00:15:45.212
because we're in the
middle of the Cold War

00:15:45.212 --> 00:15:49.350
and Congo is a place full of
tons of natural resources,

00:15:49.350 --> 00:15:51.540
including loads of uranium,

00:15:51.540 --> 00:15:53.790
the main ingredient for nuclear bombs.

00:15:53.790 --> 00:15:54.720
This is at a time when

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:57.330
Americans are keeping gas
masks next to their bed

00:15:57.330 --> 00:15:59.670
and have hordes of canned
goods in their basements.

00:15:59.670 --> 00:16:01.470
And officials in Washington can't risk

00:16:01.470 --> 00:16:04.920
Congo falling into the
influence of the Soviet Union.

00:16:04.920 --> 00:16:06.840
So they start focusing
on this prime minister.

00:16:06.840 --> 00:16:08.347
The CIA director called him, quote,

00:16:08.347 --> 00:16:11.250
"An urgent and prime
objective" that should

00:16:11.250 --> 00:16:14.580
quote, "be a high priority
of our covert action."

00:16:14.580 --> 00:16:17.670
So they pull a more political
coup than the ones before.

00:16:17.670 --> 00:16:19.950
They start allying with
Lumumbau's political enemies

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:21.930
and Congo's former colonizer, Belgium.

00:16:21.930 --> 00:16:23.370
They bribe politicians,

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:25.320
they fund protests and labor movements,

00:16:25.320 --> 00:16:26.820
and they circulate propaganda,

00:16:26.820 --> 00:16:28.890
similar ingredients to the previous coups.

00:16:28.890 --> 00:16:29.910
And when the moment is right,

00:16:29.910 --> 00:16:33.010
all these bribed politicians
do what the CIA asked them to.

00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:36.665
They'd remove Lumumba from
power, and the CIA is right there

00:16:36.665 --> 00:16:39.540
giving money and intelligence and advice

00:16:39.540 --> 00:16:40.890
to the new government.

00:16:40.890 --> 00:16:43.462
This political solution was
actually not the first try.

00:16:43.462 --> 00:16:46.522
The CIA had tried to assassinate
Lumumbau in the past,

00:16:46.522 --> 00:16:48.540
but all of those attempts failed,

00:16:48.540 --> 00:16:49.860
which is why they turned to

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:52.470
hijacking and manipulating
Congolese politics,

00:16:52.470 --> 00:16:53.880
a brand new democracy,

00:16:53.880 --> 00:16:56.010
supporting the people who
would eventually go on to

00:16:56.010 --> 00:16:57.270
put Lumumba in front of

00:16:57.270 --> 00:16:59.700
a Congolese and Belgian firing squad,

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:02.280
making this effectively
a political assassination

00:17:02.280 --> 00:17:03.960
supported from an ocean away.

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:06.690
And yet there's so much
gray area in these coups.

00:17:06.690 --> 00:17:08.550
In this case, it's really tough to prove

00:17:08.550 --> 00:17:09.825
that the CIA's support was

00:17:09.825 --> 00:17:12.601
the key factor in
Lumumbau's assassination.

00:17:12.601 --> 00:17:14.307
It's debated to this day.

00:17:14.307 --> 00:17:17.325
An effective foreign-sponsored
coup works like this,

00:17:17.325 --> 00:17:21.022
operating in the shadows,
fueling divisions,

00:17:21.022 --> 00:17:24.660
appealing to the worst demons
of the people on the ground

00:17:24.660 --> 00:17:26.673
through money, through influence.

00:17:30.210 --> 00:17:32.902
All right, let's move on to
the Caribbean in the 1960s.

00:17:32.902 --> 00:17:35.160
(urgent synth music)

00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:37.800
There's a brutal dictator here
in the Dominican Republic.

00:17:37.800 --> 00:17:38.790
I mean, this guy's really bad.

00:17:38.790 --> 00:17:41.430
He's rumored to feed
his opponents to sharks.

00:17:41.430 --> 00:17:43.380
But anyway, what the
US cares about is that

00:17:43.380 --> 00:17:45.360
there's fear that a communist revolution

00:17:45.360 --> 00:17:46.920
could happen at any moment.

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:49.410
So the CIA sends weapons
to a group of of hitmen

00:17:49.410 --> 00:17:51.150
who go assassinate this guy.

00:17:51.150 --> 00:17:53.520
It ends up being an
ambush and a car chase.

00:17:53.520 --> 00:17:55.050
They're successful in taking him out,

00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:56.763
ending his 31-year rule.

00:17:58.349 --> 00:18:02.130
And eventually the US sends
in forces to occupy the DR,

00:18:02.130 --> 00:18:04.920
to make sure that a leftist
candidate doesn't come to power.

00:18:04.920 --> 00:18:06.060
They restore order,

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:08.763
and eventually a US-friendly
candidate is elected.

00:18:10.530 --> 00:18:13.660
Okay, so now we have to head
over to Vietnam in 1963.

00:18:13.660 --> 00:18:17.280
(suspenseful string music)

00:18:17.280 --> 00:18:19.260
And boy, this is a way bigger
one than we have time for,

00:18:19.260 --> 00:18:21.600
but we're trying to focus
on the coup element of this.

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:23.310
Vietnam was divided in two,

00:18:23.310 --> 00:18:26.070
between communist and
pro-Western governments.

00:18:26.070 --> 00:18:28.830
The US needs the South
to stay on their side,

00:18:28.830 --> 00:18:31.170
but Washington starts to
lose confidence in this guy,

00:18:31.170 --> 00:18:33.870
the South's leader, he's
losing a grip on the country,

00:18:33.870 --> 00:18:35.460
and the US fears that communism will

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:37.380
take over the whole country of Vietnam.

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:40.590
So the CIA rolls up its sleeves,
it's time for another coup.

00:18:40.590 --> 00:18:43.170
This time they focus on a
South Vietnamese general

00:18:43.170 --> 00:18:45.030
who also doesn't love the president,

00:18:45.030 --> 00:18:47.130
and he agrees to do the CIA's bidding.

00:18:47.130 --> 00:18:49.630
And when given the signal, the
general directs his military

00:18:49.630 --> 00:18:52.420
to seize the airport and radio stations,

00:18:52.420 --> 00:18:54.360
and they block off highways.

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:56.220
They march to the presidential palace,

00:18:56.220 --> 00:18:57.660
a bloody shootout goes down,

00:18:57.660 --> 00:19:00.000
and this president,
President Diem, escapes.

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:01.954
He happens to be with his brother,

00:19:01.954 --> 00:19:03.510
but it's not going well for
them, so he realizes that

00:19:03.510 --> 00:19:05.580
he needs to set up a meeting to surrender.

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:07.470
They're gonna meet at a Catholic church.

00:19:07.470 --> 00:19:09.420
This was probably gonna
be a peaceful meeting,

00:19:09.420 --> 00:19:10.740
but when the generals arrive,

00:19:10.740 --> 00:19:15.740
they just kill him on
the spot, saying, quote,

00:19:15.997 --> 00:19:18.840
"To kill the weed, you
must pull up the roots."

00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:22.260
Meaning in order to solve
the problem, Diem must die.

00:19:22.260 --> 00:19:23.610
Exile was not enough.

00:19:23.610 --> 00:19:25.920
Now the US actually didn't
plan for this to happen.

00:19:25.920 --> 00:19:27.300
They didn't want to kill this guy.

00:19:27.300 --> 00:19:29.430
It was not an official
order from Washington.

00:19:29.430 --> 00:19:31.320
But they made this coup happen.

00:19:31.320 --> 00:19:33.840
JFK is said to be really
distraught about this.

00:19:33.840 --> 00:19:36.330
The first American Catholic
president behind the coup

00:19:36.330 --> 00:19:39.030
that killed the first
Vietnamese Catholic president.

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:42.600
And incidentally, JFK was
assassinated 20 days later.

00:19:42.600 --> 00:19:44.280
And one national security journalist

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:47.130
argues that Diem's
assassination actually had

00:19:47.130 --> 00:19:50.902
a greater impact on American
history than the murder of JFK

00:19:50.902 --> 00:19:52.896
because it locked the US into

00:19:52.896 --> 00:19:55.680
a decade of conflict in Vietnam,

00:19:55.680 --> 00:19:57.840
which ballooned into a long war

00:19:57.840 --> 00:19:59.790
ending in an embarrassing defeat

00:19:59.790 --> 00:20:01.470
and a political crisis at home.

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:02.730
One of the few coups where

00:20:02.730 --> 00:20:05.163
the US actually had to
deal with the aftermath.

00:20:08.380 --> 00:20:10.860
Okay, let's blast through a
few of these really quickly.

00:20:10.860 --> 00:20:12.510
I'm gonna skirt over some details here.

00:20:12.510 --> 00:20:14.400
It's 1964, and Brazil is

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:16.320
potentially veering off into communism,

00:20:16.320 --> 00:20:18.000
with the rise of a new leftist leader.

00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:19.110
Lucky for the CIA,

00:20:19.110 --> 00:20:21.060
there's already a coup
being plotted against him.

00:20:21.060 --> 00:20:22.830
So the US military just
shows up with ships

00:20:22.830 --> 00:20:23.940
off the coast of Brazil.

00:20:23.940 --> 00:20:26.525
They airlift in a bunch of
ammunition and supplies.

00:20:26.525 --> 00:20:28.950
They didn't end up having
to do much, actually.

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:31.380
Instead, they just stood
by with reinforcements

00:20:31.380 --> 00:20:33.840
and watched the Brazilian coup go down.

00:20:33.840 --> 00:20:37.230
The leftist leader goes down
and a new leader comes in.

00:20:37.230 --> 00:20:39.420
In 1973, there's a coup in Chile

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:42.360
that is a very complicated
story with conflicting accounts

00:20:42.360 --> 00:20:44.610
and we went down a super deep rabbit hole

00:20:44.610 --> 00:20:45.750
and we've decided that

00:20:45.750 --> 00:20:48.150
because the evidence is not rock solid,

00:20:48.150 --> 00:20:49.830
we're going to cut it for time,

00:20:49.830 --> 00:20:51.480
but definitely some crazy shit went down,

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:52.809
I'm not saying it didn't.

00:20:52.809 --> 00:20:56.850
(urgent jazz drum music)

00:20:56.850 --> 00:20:58.800
Okay, we're back in Africa
and it's the eighties.

00:20:58.800 --> 00:21:01.710
And over here in Libya, the
dictator Muammar Gaddafi

00:21:01.710 --> 00:21:03.540
was making lots of trouble in the region,

00:21:03.540 --> 00:21:04.650
funding terrorist groups

00:21:04.650 --> 00:21:07.500
and working to expand his
influence all over the region.

00:21:07.500 --> 00:21:09.269
Then he gets a call from his neighbor Chad

00:21:09.269 --> 00:21:11.615
asking for help against a rebellion.

00:21:11.615 --> 00:21:13.835
Gaddafi eagerly sends 4,000 troops

00:21:13.835 --> 00:21:16.020
to occupy a huge part of the country

00:21:16.020 --> 00:21:17.610
and makes friends with the new president

00:21:17.610 --> 00:21:19.323
by helping him exile his rival.

00:21:20.165 --> 00:21:20.998
And soon Gaddafi is getting greedy

00:21:20.998 --> 00:21:23.610
and threatening to merge Chad into Libya.

00:21:23.610 --> 00:21:25.770
The US is not into this.

00:21:25.770 --> 00:21:28.632
So Ronald Reagan fires up
the well-oiled coup machine,

00:21:28.632 --> 00:21:30.240
launching a covert war,

00:21:30.240 --> 00:21:32.700
sending weapons and
cash to rebels in Chad,

00:21:32.700 --> 00:21:35.130
and supporting that political
opponent who was ousted,

00:21:35.130 --> 00:21:37.230
helping him fight back, and it works.

00:21:37.230 --> 00:21:38.790
The president of Chad has to flee

00:21:38.790 --> 00:21:41.089
and the US backed and
supported leader comes to power

00:21:41.089 --> 00:21:42.780
and now there's a conflict,

00:21:42.780 --> 00:21:44.850
and the CIA continues arming the war

00:21:44.850 --> 00:21:46.980
even after this guy is in office.

00:21:46.980 --> 00:21:50.070
The new US-backed leader
rules brutally for eight years

00:21:50.070 --> 00:21:52.440
until he's eventually overthrown
by a military officer.

00:21:52.440 --> 00:21:55.329
And in 2013, he was charged
with crimes against humanity,

00:21:55.329 --> 00:21:57.543
torture and war crimes.

00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:05.000
Okay, now let's go to this
little island in 1983.

00:22:05.000 --> 00:22:06.450
(percussive jazz music)

00:22:06.450 --> 00:22:09.420
It's communism again, and
the US sends 2,000 troops

00:22:09.420 --> 00:22:11.640
to invade this small remote island

00:22:11.640 --> 00:22:13.410
and remove their communist leader.

00:22:13.410 --> 00:22:15.720
They didn't really know much
about this small island,

00:22:15.720 --> 00:22:18.030
and they literally had to use tourism maps

00:22:18.030 --> 00:22:20.190
to plan their invasion. Anyway.

00:22:20.190 --> 00:22:22.740
American forces move in,
overwhelm the Grenadian fighters

00:22:22.740 --> 00:22:24.990
who happen to be joined
by their Cuban allies,

00:22:24.990 --> 00:22:26.010
the government collapses

00:22:26.010 --> 00:22:28.173
and the US-friendly leader comes to power.

00:22:32.260 --> 00:22:33.930
Okay, back down to Central America.

00:22:33.930 --> 00:22:36.150
It's 1989 and we're here in Panama

00:22:36.150 --> 00:22:39.420
where the US has control
of a very important canal.

00:22:39.420 --> 00:22:41.760
And luckily the Panamanian
dictator has been

00:22:41.760 --> 00:22:43.830
very friendly to American interests.

00:22:43.830 --> 00:22:46.080
But the US starts losing
confidence in this guy,

00:22:46.080 --> 00:22:48.330
wondering if he's really the best choice,

00:22:48.330 --> 00:22:51.960
ensuring the US maintain easy
access to their vital canal.

00:22:51.960 --> 00:22:54.960
Oh, and it didn't help that
this guy was indicted in Florida

00:22:54.960 --> 00:22:58.170
on drug trafficking and
money laundering charges.

00:22:58.170 --> 00:22:59.550
We gotta get him out.

00:22:59.550 --> 00:23:01.590
But the straw that broke the
camel's back for this guy was

00:23:01.590 --> 00:23:03.120
when Panamanian troops killed

00:23:03.120 --> 00:23:05.400
an unarmed American
soldier in Panama City.

00:23:05.400 --> 00:23:06.930
The US is done with this guy,

00:23:06.930 --> 00:23:10.320
so they invade Panama with 27,000 troops.

00:23:10.320 --> 00:23:11.850
Panama's military is crushed

00:23:11.850 --> 00:23:13.661
and the dictator is eventually arrested

00:23:13.661 --> 00:23:16.200
and sentenced to 40 years in prison,

00:23:16.200 --> 00:23:19.143
and the US ensures access
to its canal after all.

00:23:24.046 --> 00:23:26.508
Okay, so now it's the end of the 1980s

00:23:26.508 --> 00:23:29.439
and the Soviets are invading Afghanistan

00:23:29.439 --> 00:23:32.340
(urgent string music)

00:23:32.340 --> 00:23:34.560
and are meeting resistance
from a bunch of fighters

00:23:34.560 --> 00:23:36.780
from all over the world who
have come to Afghanistan

00:23:36.780 --> 00:23:39.180
to fight back against
the Soviet occupation,

00:23:39.180 --> 00:23:42.180
many of them with fundamentalist
religious motivations.

00:23:42.180 --> 00:23:44.370
But the US doesn't care
about their motivation.

00:23:44.370 --> 00:23:46.170
They just care that that
they're willing to fight

00:23:46.170 --> 00:23:47.280
against the Soviets

00:23:47.280 --> 00:23:49.920
and the Soviets' puppet,
the Afghan president.

00:23:49.920 --> 00:23:51.270
And it totally works.

00:23:51.270 --> 00:23:52.410
With the help of the US,

00:23:52.410 --> 00:23:54.480
these fighters push the Soviets back

00:23:54.480 --> 00:23:57.420
and successfully run the
Afghan president out of office.

00:23:57.420 --> 00:23:59.190
And as he's being run out of office,

00:23:59.190 --> 00:24:01.285
he forebodingly warns the Americans that

00:24:01.285 --> 00:24:04.050
if they leave Afghanistan in
the hands of these fighters,

00:24:04.050 --> 00:24:05.557
that it would, quote,

00:24:05.557 --> 00:24:08.070
"Be turned into a center for terrorism."

00:24:08.070 --> 00:24:11.310
And his prophecy was completely fulfilled.

00:24:11.310 --> 00:24:13.620
Those US-funded fighters were people

00:24:13.620 --> 00:24:16.680
whose names we know
today: Osama bin Laden,

00:24:16.680 --> 00:24:19.380
Abu Musab Al-Zarqawi, the
guy who started the group

00:24:19.380 --> 00:24:21.300
that would eventually become ISIS.

00:24:21.300 --> 00:24:24.630
Those same weapons that the
US sent to counter the Soviets

00:24:24.630 --> 00:24:27.147
and to effect regime change in Afghanistan

00:24:27.147 --> 00:24:30.660
would go on to be used against
American soldiers years later

00:24:30.660 --> 00:24:31.704
when the US was back

00:24:31.704 --> 00:24:35.044
orchestrating yet another
regime change after 9/11

00:24:35.044 --> 00:24:37.920
against the very groups they once enabled.

00:24:37.920 --> 00:24:40.920
The US would eventually leave
Afghanistan, only to find

00:24:40.920 --> 00:24:44.133
the country immediately
falling back into Taliban rule.

00:24:45.000 --> 00:24:46.260
We're almost to the end of our list

00:24:46.260 --> 00:24:48.725
and we're now in modern day, it's 2003,

00:24:48.725 --> 00:24:51.693
and 150,000 American troops invade Iraq.

00:24:52.710 --> 00:24:55.200
They say that they are
there to find and destroy

00:24:55.200 --> 00:24:57.060
weapons of mass destruction,

00:24:57.060 --> 00:25:00.180
but their main focus is taking
out this guy, Saddam Hussein,

00:25:00.180 --> 00:25:02.190
which they do in a matter of weeks.

00:25:02.190 --> 00:25:03.810
Saddam fleeing into hiding

00:25:03.810 --> 00:25:06.780
and President Bush declaring
"mission accomplished,"

00:25:06.780 --> 00:25:09.510
establishing an American-friendly
government in Iraq,

00:25:09.510 --> 00:25:11.270
creating once again a negative byproduct

00:25:11.270 --> 00:25:15.060
by alienating huge swaths
of the Iraqi people and army

00:25:15.060 --> 00:25:17.760
who form a bunch of
anti-American rebel groups

00:25:17.760 --> 00:25:20.190
that go on to fight against
the American occupation,

00:25:20.190 --> 00:25:22.350
some morphing into groups like ISIS

00:25:22.350 --> 00:25:26.160
who wreak all kinds of havoc
on the region to this day.

00:25:26.160 --> 00:25:28.710
Once again, I made a whole
video about this topic.

00:25:28.710 --> 00:25:29.640
Go check it out.

00:25:29.640 --> 00:25:32.880
Iraq remains a place of
deep political instability.

00:25:32.880 --> 00:25:35.280
Trust in government is extremely low.

00:25:35.280 --> 00:25:38.280
And the question of
how and why we did this

00:25:38.280 --> 00:25:41.190
expensive, horrific, destructive coup

00:25:41.190 --> 00:25:44.880
is still something that there
aren't really good answers to.

00:25:44.880 --> 00:25:47.267
Again, you can go watch
my video for more on that.

00:25:47.267 --> 00:25:48.480
(pensive piano music)

00:25:48.480 --> 00:25:50.760
And this gets us to the
final coup on our list.

00:25:50.760 --> 00:25:53.160
It's 2011, during a wave of protests

00:25:53.160 --> 00:25:54.630
spreading throughout this region,

00:25:54.630 --> 00:25:57.300
trying to take down all
these strongmen dictators,

00:25:57.300 --> 00:25:59.670
one of which was this guy Muammar Gaddafi.

00:25:59.670 --> 00:26:02.070
The same Gaddafi we were
talking about earlier

00:26:02.070 --> 00:26:03.720
who was like taking over Chad?

00:26:03.720 --> 00:26:06.870
He's still here and he's
still a very horrible dude.

00:26:06.870 --> 00:26:08.640
And there's worry that
he's gonna potentially

00:26:08.640 --> 00:26:11.520
massacre all of these
pro-democracy protestors.

00:26:11.520 --> 00:26:13.530
So the US feels like it must get involved

00:26:13.530 --> 00:26:15.210
to save these protestors.

00:26:15.210 --> 00:26:17.550
They rally their NATO allies to help them,

00:26:17.550 --> 00:26:19.380
but at some point the mission switches

00:26:19.380 --> 00:26:21.090
to total regime change.

00:26:21.090 --> 00:26:23.245
We don't know exactly how this happened,

00:26:23.245 --> 00:26:24.866
only the people in the room do.

00:26:24.866 --> 00:26:26.700
But is it surprising?

00:26:26.700 --> 00:26:29.765
We've seen this long arc
of the US using the coup

00:26:29.765 --> 00:26:32.400
as a force for getting their way

00:26:32.400 --> 00:26:34.200
in an international conflict.

00:26:34.200 --> 00:26:35.340
It's a tried and true tool

00:26:35.340 --> 00:26:37.350
in the American foreign policy toolkit.

00:26:37.350 --> 00:26:40.470
So it's not surprising that
a coup becomes a solution

00:26:40.470 --> 00:26:43.110
during these difficult
decision-making processes.

00:26:43.110 --> 00:26:45.450
So anyway, the target becomes Gaddafi,

00:26:45.450 --> 00:26:48.840
and now NATO drones are
firing missiles at his convoy

00:26:48.840 --> 00:26:52.050
and he eventually gets captured
and gets killed on the spot.

00:26:52.050 --> 00:26:54.300
Libya has been in chaos ever since,

00:26:54.300 --> 00:26:56.640
but it's not like it was a
great place under Gaddafi.

00:26:56.640 --> 00:26:58.230
And once again, we're in a gray area where

00:26:58.230 --> 00:27:00.210
we don't know the history
that didn't happen

00:27:00.210 --> 00:27:02.100
or how things could have
turned out different

00:27:02.100 --> 00:27:04.170
if the US didn't get involved.

00:27:04.170 --> 00:27:05.523
That debate lives on.

00:27:07.170 --> 00:27:08.970
Okay, so that's our list.

00:27:08.970 --> 00:27:10.110
These are our coups

00:27:10.110 --> 00:27:12.240
that we decided to go over in this video.

00:27:12.240 --> 00:27:14.610
And there are so many more
that we could have mentioned.

00:27:14.610 --> 00:27:17.790
My purpose in doing this
broad back-to-back history

00:27:17.790 --> 00:27:19.590
of American led coups

00:27:19.590 --> 00:27:22.230
was so that we can see
patterns that emerge.

00:27:22.230 --> 00:27:23.580
How a rising superpower

00:27:23.580 --> 00:27:25.980
became really good at removing leaders

00:27:25.980 --> 00:27:28.560
that didn't align with their
way of seeing the world

00:27:28.560 --> 00:27:29.790
or, in a lot of cases,

00:27:29.790 --> 00:27:32.430
who were not friendly to
American business interests.

00:27:32.430 --> 00:27:34.920
But let's be clear, the
US didn't invent this.

00:27:34.920 --> 00:27:35.753
This is something that

00:27:35.753 --> 00:27:38.220
powerful countries and
empires have always done.

00:27:38.220 --> 00:27:40.020
What characterizes US-led coups,

00:27:40.020 --> 00:27:41.550
especially during the Cold War,

00:27:41.550 --> 00:27:43.440
was how the overthrow of these governments

00:27:43.440 --> 00:27:45.869
often stamped out new democracies,

00:27:45.869 --> 00:27:48.060
budding democratic movements,

00:27:48.060 --> 00:27:50.520
replacing them with authoritarian leaders

00:27:50.520 --> 00:27:52.860
who would go on to oppress the people

00:27:52.860 --> 00:27:55.740
with the support and backing
of the United States,

00:27:55.740 --> 00:27:58.980
and in the process, redirecting
the country's history.

00:27:58.980 --> 00:28:00.970
Lately, Russia has been meddling in

00:28:00.970 --> 00:28:03.870
the election process of the United States,

00:28:03.870 --> 00:28:06.390
and I've been reflecting on
my feelings towards that.

00:28:06.390 --> 00:28:09.450
The violation of having an external power

00:28:09.450 --> 00:28:12.330
sowing doubt and polarization and fear

00:28:12.330 --> 00:28:14.874
in my own democracy, in my own society.

00:28:14.874 --> 00:28:18.046
It feels like such a violation, and it is.

00:28:18.046 --> 00:28:21.660
This is giving me just a tiny
taste of what it feels like

00:28:21.660 --> 00:28:23.250
to have an outside power

00:28:23.250 --> 00:28:25.170
pulling this strings in your country,

00:28:25.170 --> 00:28:27.990
tearing it apart for their own purposes,

00:28:27.990 --> 00:28:31.200
and in the process, creating
more problems for the people

00:28:31.200 --> 00:28:33.240
and for the United States itself,

00:28:33.240 --> 00:28:37.165
undermining any semblance
of democracy or development,

00:28:37.165 --> 00:28:40.061
all in the name of keeping the US on top

00:28:40.061 --> 00:28:41.943
and dominant over the globe.

00:28:42.906 --> 00:28:46.239
(wistful ambient music)

